[Applause]  three of the top producers at the ellen  degeneres show are  out amid a workplace misconduct  investigation at the daytime talk show  a spokesperson for warner brothers  confirms to et  that executive producers ed glavin and  kevin lehmann  and co-executive producer jonathan  norman have parted ways with the program  e.t has also learned that derrick  westervelt mary connolly  and andy lassner will remain at the show  as executive producers  alongside ellen house dj steven twitch  boss has  also been named co-executive producer in  recent months  her character has been called into  question what do you say to those  critics  i have personally seen all the love that  she puts in  in the world so it's just like people  just people just got time  you know people got time so i mean we'll  always try to tear people that are on  top down  yeah e.t has learned that news of the  shake-up was delivered to the staff  on monday during a zoom meeting where  the 62-year-old talk show host  apologized to anyone whose feelings were  hurt  i you know i think that i was a nice  person to begin with and i hope i've  gotten nicer  ellen also acknowledged that mistakes  were made before noting how grateful she  is for her team  i stay grateful and i try to stay humble  and i think that i  pay attention to what is important and  what is real and in addition to all of  that  e.t has learned that hr changes were  also announced to help improve the work  environment  and the employee experience at the show  of course this whole thing started back  in july after buzzfeed  news published an article which included  anonymous accounts of misconduct at the  show  from a dozen former and one current  employee  glavin lehmann and norman were all cited  in the article and were reportedly  suspended  at the time warner brothers television  sent an internal memo to staff  informing them that an independent  third-party firm would be hired to  interview  current and former employees about their  experiences behind the scenes  and in an internal letter sent to the  show's staff obtained by et  ellen apologized and said she was  committed to having conversations about  fairness and justice i don't think you  achieve anything by  by bullying people e.t has also learned  that the workplace investigation  is still ongoing and a source close to  the team  says that ellen's main priority right  now is the staff  i started out as a comedian and i wanted  to make people laugh and i wanted to  make people happy and feel good

